  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Accommodation Facilities II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will ensure that unaccompanied migrant children (UMC) identified in precarious living conditions have immediate access to accommodation and assistance tailored to their best interest. This will be achieved through a two-fold approach, addressing both the UMC&#x2019;s needs as well as the provision of technical support to the competent authorities to fulfil their duties. Specifically, on the population side, the project foresees the operation of the EAFs where UMC will be hosted upon their identification and referral by the NERM and until their placement to other long-term accommodation schemes or other long-term care arrangements. On the institutional side, the SGVP&#x2019; s capacity in linking the EAFs with long-term solutions will be enhanced through the provision of technical support and specialized staff.</narrative>
  </description>
